{{if .ServesPrompts}}`mark_worlds` on every other connected MCP server that offers it; a failure: surface it, skip that server. One reporting `system: <host>` is a `knowledge` destination, `<host>` its identity, reached through that server's own tools; none: `NONE`.{{else}}Bash: `"$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" registry detect-promote -hosts`. Non-zero exit or malformed output: surface, stop. One destination per line: `knowledge <slug> [<host>]` (brokered system, `<host>` its identity) or `target <slug> <path> [label]` (plain endpoint with its declared write `<path>`), reached through {{.ToolForm}} of that slug; or `NONE`.{{end}}